<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gustáv Husák</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1913–1991</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gustáv Husák was a Slovak communist who was imprisoned in the 1950s but rehabilitated in the 1960s. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw-pact">Warsaw Pact</a> invasion he replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-dubcek">Alexander Dubček</a> as party leader in 1969 and presided over the period of normalisation, with purges and censorship. He was also president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> from 1975 until he resigned in December 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gustav-husak.jpg" alt="Gustáv Husák" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: http://kalendarakcii.bratislava.sk/vismo/akce.asp?id_org=700021&amp;amp;id=4789&amp;amp;p1=7765 http://zpravy.idnes.cz/foto.a... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gust%C3%A1v_Hus%C3%A1k_-_o%C5%99%C3%ADznuto.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
